=== config hot-reload apply pattern ===
274:/// Data returned by `apply_payload_to_config` for a deferred `instance_id_map` merge.
275-///
276-/// Contains:
277-/// - The set of `instance_id` strings that were in the OLD `cfg.disk_allowlist`
278-///   (needed to determine which entries to remove from the map).
279-/// - The new `Vec<DiskIdentity>` from the server payload (entries to insert/overwrite).
280-///
281-/// `None` is returned when `disk_allowlist` did not change (no merge needed).
282-type DiskMergeData = Option<(
283-    std::collections::HashSet<String>,
284-    Vec<dlp_common::DiskIdentity>,
285-)>;
286-
287-/// Diffs a server-pushed `AgentConfigPayload` against in-memory `AgentConfig`
288-/// and applies all detected changes including the `disk_allowlist` merge.
289-///
290-/// Extracted as a standalone synchronous function so tests can invoke the
291-/// diff/merge logic directly without spinning up a full async polling loop.
292-///
293-/// # Design: config lock BEFORE enumerator lock (T-37-13)
294-///
295-/// This function expects that the config mutex is already held by the caller
296-/// and that the enumerator is accessed AFTER the function returns (i.e., AFTER
297-/// the config lock is released). To preserve this invariant the function returns
298-/// any data needed for the deferred enumerator merge: the old instance_id set
299-/// and the new list. The caller then does the map merge with the config lock dropped.
300-///
301-/// # Arguments
302-///
303-/// * `cfg` — mutable borrow of the in-memory agent config (config mutex held
304-///   by the caller).
--
